{"status":"ready","content":"I need to find the determinant of this 4×4 matrix. Let me multiply through by common denominators to simplify.\r\n\r\nThe matrix is:\r\n$$A = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -\\frac{9}{2} & -\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{3} & \\frac{25}{6} & -\\frac{19}{6} & \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{23}{6} & \\frac{29}{6} & -\\frac{10}{3} & -\\frac{19}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{6} & -\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{7}{3} \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\nMultiply all entries by 6 to get matrix B (so det(A) = det(B)/6⁴ = det(B)/1296):\r\n\r\n$$B = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 & 6 & -27 & -26 \\\\ -26 & 25 & -19 & 11 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 15 & 14 \\end{pmatrix}$$\r\n\r\nI'll expand using cofactor expansion along row 1.\r\n\r\n**Computing the 3×3 minors:**\r\n\r\n**M₁₁:** (rows 2,3,4; cols 2,3,4)\r\n$$\\begin{vmatrix} 25 & -19 & 11 \\\\ 29 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -7 & 15 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n= 25(-20·14 - (-19)·15) - (-19)(29·14 - (-19)·(-7)) + 11(29·15 - (-20)·(-7))\r\n= 25(-280 + 285) + 19(406 - 133) + 11(435 - 140)\r\n= 25(5) + 19(273) + 11(295) = 125 + 5187 + 3245 = 8557\r\n\r\n**M₁₂:** (rows 2,3,4; cols 1,3,4)\r\n$$\\begin{vmatrix} -26 & -19 & 11 \\\\ -23 & -20 & -19 \\\\ -17 & 15 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n= -26(-20·14 - (-19)·15) + 19(-23·14 - (-19)·(-17)) + 11(-23·15 - (-20)·(-17))\r\n= -26(-280+285) + 19(-322-323) + 11(-345-340)\r\n= -26(5) + 19(-645) + 11(-685) = -130 - 12255 - 7535 = -19920\r\n\r\n**M₁₃:** (rows 2,3,4; cols 1,2,4)\r\n$$\\begin{vmatrix} -26 & 25 & 11 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -19 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 14 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n= -26(29·14 - (-19)·(-7)) - 25(-23·14 - (-19)·(-17)) + 11(-23·(-7) - 29·(-17))\r\n= -26(406-133) - 25(-322-323) + 11(161+493)\r\n= -26(273) - 25(-645) + 11(654) = -7098 + 16125 + 7194 = 16221\r\n\r\n**M₁₄:** (rows 2,3,4; cols 1,2,3)\r\n$$\\begin{vmatrix} -26 & 25 & -19 \\\\ -23 & 29 & -20 \\\\ -17 & -7 & 15 \\end{vmatrix}$$\r\n= -26(29·15 - (-20)·(-7)) - 25(-23·15 - (-20)·(-17)) + (-19)(-23·(-7) - 29·(-17))\r\n= -26(435-140) - 25(-345-340) - 19(161+493)\r\n= -26(295) - 25(-685) - 19(654) = -7670 + 17125 - 12426 = -2971\r\n\r\n**det(B):**\r\n= 8(8557) - 6(-19920) + (-27)(16221) + (-26)(-2971)\r\n= 68456 + 119520 - 437967 + 77246\r\n= 68456 + 119520 + 77246 - 437967\r\n= 265222 - 437967 = -172745\r\n\r\n**det(A) = -172745/1296**\r\n\r\nLet me check if this simplifies: GCD(172745, 1296). 1296 = 2⁴·3⁴. 172745 is odd, so no common factors with 2. 1+7+2+7+4+5 = 26, not divisible by 3. So the fraction is already simplified.\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{-\\dfrac{172745}{1296}}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-6/livebench-057-math.txt","size":2415,"mtime":1779367184}